(Title) Tj
T*
(Osmotic Laxative Adjunct to Multimodal Recovery Pathway Accelerates Postoperative) Tj
T*
(Gastrointestinal Recovery After Hysterectomy: A Randomized Effectiveness Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Enhanced recovery pathways address multiple perioperative factors, yet bowel dysfunction) Tj
T*
(remains common after abdominal surgery. We evaluated whether addition of an osmotic agent) Tj
T*
(to a standardized enhanced recovery protocol improves gastrointestinal outcomes. We) Tj
T*
(randomized 160 women \(mean age 52 years\) undergoing hysterectomy to receive either) Tj
T*
(enhanced recovery care with oral osmotic laxative \(n=80\) or enhanced recovery care without) Tj
T*
(additional intervention \(n=80\). The osmotic-supplemented group received laxative doses) Tj
T*
(beginning immediately after surgery. Primary outcome was time to tolerance of regular) Tj
T*
(diet, assessed via nursing assessment and patient report. Secondary outcomes included) Tj
T*
(rates of clinically significant bowel dysfunction, time to first bowel movement, and) Tj
T*
(patient-reported comfort. Median time to dietary advancement was significantly shorter in) Tj
T*
(the osmotic group \(20.8 hours vs. 29.1 hours; p<0.001\). Clinically significant bowel) Tj
T*
(dysfunction occurred in 3.8% of the osmotic group versus 27.5% of the control group) Tj
T*
(\(p<0.001\). Time to flatus was reduced in the osmotic group \(17.2 hours vs. 22.4 hours;) Tj
T*
(p<0.001\). Patient satisfaction with recovery was higher in the osmotic-supplemented arm) Tj
T*
(\(p<0.001\).) Tj
